# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Better Call Kanoon - Docker build context exclusions.
#
# This file is not optional. Without it, `COPY frontend/ ./` in the Dockerfile's
# node stage copies the HOST's node_modules over the Linux ones that `npm ci`
# just installed. On a Windows host that means win32 binaries landing on top of
# linux-gnu binaries, and `vite build` fails inside the image. It also bloats
# the 88 MB dependency tree into the build context on every single build.
#
# Same story for `.venv`: without this exclusion the entire Windows virtualenv
# (every .pyd and .dll in site-packages) is shipped to the daemon on each build.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# --- Secrets ---------------------------------------------------------------
# Never let a real .env reach the daemon, the build cache, or an image layer.
.env
.env.*
**/.env
**/.env.*
!.env.example
!**/.env.example

# --- Host dependency trees -------------------------------------------------
# The node stage runs `npm ci` itself, from package-lock.json, so it always
# installs for the TARGET platform rather than the host's.
node_modules
**/node_modules

# --- Host virtualenvs ------------------------------------------------------
# The python stage runs `pip install -r requirements.txt` itself.
.venv
**/.venv
venv
**/venv
env
**/env

# --- Build output (regenerated inside the image) ---------------------------
# frontend/dist is produced by the node stage; copying the host's copy in
# would shadow it and could mask a stale local build.
dist
**/dist
build
**/build

# --- Caches ----------------------------------------------------------------
__pycache__
**/__pycache__
*.py[cod]
.pytest_cache
**/.pytest_cache
.ruff_cache
**/.ruff_cache
.mypy_cache
**/.mypy_cache
*.egg-info
**/*.egg-info

# --- VCS, CI and editor metadata -------------------------------------------
.git
.gitignore
.github
.vscode
.idea
.claude
*.swp
*.swo
*~

# --- OS cruft --------------------------------------------------------------
.DS_Store
._*
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini

# --- Docs and assets the image does not need -------------------------------
# The README documents local development; it has no place in a runtime image.
*.md
!backend/**/*.md